      "path": "app/src/main/java/tv/own/owntv/kevbox/live/LiveVideoStage.kt",
      "content": "This clears the Sports box on any section change while `playerMode != NONE`, MINI included. That is wider than the launcher-tile case it was written for. Example: a user opens the Sports box channel full screen, shrinks it to the mini-player and browses to Home. The box is wiped. Back on Sports, a full-screen Back no longer hands the stream back to the box (`isBackToGrid` needs `boxSection == SPORTS`), so the stream stops. Live TV and Search boxes keep their box in this same flow. Consider narrowing the condition to the case where the playing channel isn't the box's channel, for example by passing `playingChannelId != boxChannel?.id` from the shell, or to FULLSCREEN opened from outside the box. Also add tests for the MINI case and for non-idle with a Live TV box.",
      "existing_code": "            clearBox = boxSection == MainSection.SPORTS \u0026\u0026 section != MainSection.SPORTS,",
      "start_line": 147,
      "end_line": 147,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "app/src/main/java/tv/own/owntv/kevbox/sports/FootballListings.kt",
      "content": "The list of linked sports now lives in two places: this guard and the `when` in `link()`. If someone adds a sport to `LISTED_SPORTS` but not to the `when` (or the reverse), the two drift apart without any error. `link()` already returns null for any sport it doesn't handle, so you can drop this guard and let `link()` decide, or keep the guard and check a precomputed `Set`. If you keep it as is, `values` is a linear lookup on every call.",
      "existing_code": "        if (match.sport !in LISTED_SPORTS.values) return null",
      "start_line": 68,
      "end_line": 68,
      "category": "maintainability",
      "severity": "low"
    },
    {
